WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.323
Consider a load followed by an independent add.

2
00:00:03.323 --> 00:00:07.211
If memory is slow, the add may return its result first.

3
00:00:07.211 --> 00:00:11.170
That does not make CVA6 an out-of-order-issue processor.

4
00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:17.744
The scoreboard tracks each outstanding instruction, and commit preserves architectural order.

5
00:00:17.744 --> 00:00:22.905
Dependencies, occupied units and memory delays can all reduce throughput.

6
00:00:22.905 --> 00:00:29.196
Likewise, two issue ports are a structural capability, not a guaranteed instruction rate.

7
00:00:29.196 --> 00:00:35.700
Keep issue width, result completion and retirement separate when reading performance claims.

